less they adjust Red Sox fans or Yankees fans. They become individuals who happen to support those sports teams, individuals with a great many aspects to their identity. Sometimes it's helpful to even just imagine the details of other people's lives in order to stop seeing them purely in terms of their group identity. Mina Sessi was reminded about the power of doing this one time at work when she got an urgent text from her sister. I'm sitting in a faculty meeting and I get a text and I look down and it's from my sister so I opened it.

